2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] Palo Alto Networks (PANW) has returned 71.4% over the past year and trades about 15% below its 52-week high. You can be paid now for agreeing to buy the shares well below today's price, and you keep that payment either way. The catch: the stock has to fall a long way first, and the slowdown management has already guided to is in the growth measures, not in the company total.  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] 13% annualized yield at a 29% margin of safety, by selling put options.  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] Sell a put option on PANW expiring 9/17/2027, with a strike price of $240.  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] Collect roughly $2,128 in premium per contract (each contract covers 100 shares).  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] That works out to about 8.6% annualized on the $24,000 of cash you set aside to secure the trade.  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] Park that cash in Treasury bills or a Treasury money-market fund yielding roughly 3.9%, and your total yield climbs to about 12.6%.  
2026-09-11 09:20:49 EDT [CRAWLER] And if PANW falls below $240, you buy it at $240, an effective entry near $218.73 a share after the premium, about a 35% discount to today's $336.98.  
